---
/**
 * Port of casestudy/avito.html. Typo fixes per the plan: "Avit's" ->
 * "Avito's" (Overview) and "Mair.ru" -> "Mail.ru" (the Goal stats table).
 *
 * `.details-grid-two` table under "Goal" -> StatsList (which already owns
 * the divider the source places directly above it). Every inline `<h5>`
 * sub-heading in the Solution section -> `<Eyebrow as="h3">` (next heading
 * level down from the section's own `<h2>`, and the plan's fix for the
 * site-wide misused-`<h5>` pattern). Mid-content `.spacer-2` divs between
 * Solution sub-topics become a token-driven spacer div (`--space-section`,
 * matching `ContentBlock`'s own top-of-section spacing rhythm).
 */
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import ContentBlock from '../../components/ContentBlock.astro';
import ContentMedia from '../../components/ContentMedia.astro';
import StatsList from '../../components/StatsList.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../../components/Eyebrow.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Avito — career start case study · Jury Alyavdin"
  description="How I designed the vacancy-search experience that helps young applicants start a career through the Avito iOS app."
  path="/casestudy/avito.html"
  h1="How to start a career with Avito App"
  avatarImage="/casestudy/avito/avito-logo.png"
  orbitTop="Avito"
  orbitBottom="C2C Marketplace"
  glow="#f8f8f8"
  heroImage="/casestudy/avito/avito-hero.png"
  details={[
    { label: 'Platform', value: 'iOS' },
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Product Designer' },
    { label: 'Date', value: '2019' },
  ]}
>
  <ContentBlock title="Overview">
    <p>
      Avito.ru is a Russian classified advertisements website with sections devoted to general goods for sale,
      jobs, real estate, personals, cars for sale, and services.
    </p>
    <p>
      Avito.ru is the most popular classifieds site in Russia and is the second biggest classifieds site in the
      world after Craigslist. In January 2019, it had more than 10.3 million unique daily visitors. On average,
      Avito's users post more than 500,000 new ads daily and the overall ads are about 50 million active listings.
    </p>
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Problem">
    <p>
      At the beginning of the career, every job seems similar: low requirements, similar salary, and no one expect
      even experienced candidates. But those roles have different development prospects and different demands in
      the future.
    </p>
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Goal">
    <p>
      So how to make a way to start a career easier? How to make a job-hunting more convenient? How can the
      applicant choose from a huge number of similar vacancies? How even to choose between different areas of work?
    </p>
    <p>According to the NAFI research respondents used to search for work in Avito in most cases.</p>
    <StatsList
      items={[
        { label: 'Avito.ru', value: '36' },
        { label: 'HeadHunter (hh.ru)', value: '14' },
        { label: 'Job.ru', value: '14' },
        { label: 'SuperJob', value: '8' },
        { label: 'Zarplata.ru', value: '6' },
        { label: 'Mail.ru', value: '6' },
        { label: 'Careerist.ru', value: '5' },
        { label: 'Other', value: '1' },
        { label: 'Do not use any', value: '3' },
      ]}
    />
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Audience segmentation">
    <p>
      An applicant is an aspiring blue-collar from 18 to 25 yo. He is looking for his first job to choose his
      career path. The salary, the location of work and the quick access are the most important conditions.
    </p>
    <ContentMedia
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-profile.png"
      alt="Avito applicant profile screen"
      width={1456}
      height={968}
    />
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Competitive Analysis Report">
    <p>
      Traditional methods of job search in Russia include using employment office services, advertising and
      newspaper ads, special HR agencies, direct contact with the employer, specialized websites, social networks,
      professionally-oriented social networks, and recommendations of friends.
    </p>
    <p>The main part of the market is occupied by large local players.</p>
    <ContentMedia
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-research.png"
      alt="Competitive analysis of Russian job-search platforms"
      width={1880}
      height={1488}
    />
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Customer Journey">
    <p>So I applied the obtained qualitative studies of the user experience of employment in CJM.</p>
    <ContentMedia
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-cjm.jpg"
      alt="Customer journey map of an Avito job applicant"
      width={3167}
      height={1262}
    />
    <p>This practice helped to identify some of the applicant's pain points</p>
    <ul class="circle-list">
      <li>Have to start a career immediately, otherwise, it will be too late</li>
      <li>Don't know how to make a CV</li>
      <li>Spends a lot of time to search</li>
      <li>Receives a lot of rejections, that makes give up</li>
      <li>Fear of interviews</li>
    </ul>
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Wireframes">
    <p>
      Then I considered the possible entry points to the directory with vacancies from the application Avito.
      There were two of them in the existing application.
    </p>
    <ContentMedia
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-wireframe.png"
      alt="Early wireframes for the vacancy directory entry points"
      width={2727}
      height={1813}
    />
    <p>
      The first one included the search case: when an applicant already passed the stage of determining the
      specialty and was looking for a job according to the specified parameters.
    </p>
    <p>
      And the second was a discovery flow. When the applicant with the help of the directory got to the main
      screen of the category with vacant posts.
    </p>
  </ContentBlock>

  <ContentBlock title="Solution">
    <Eyebrow as="h3">Copy friend's CV</Eyebrow>
    <p>
      Usually, the applicant begins to realize the need for employment immediately after graduation (at the time
      of graduation). He is overcome by the fear of being out of work at an early stage.
    </p>
    <p>
      The social factor strongly influences the definition of a career. So there is a hypothesis that access to
      the resume of friends from the contact list can help the decision to choose a role.
    </p>
    <ContentMedia
      kind="video"
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-contacts"
      alt="Prototype of copying a friend's CV from the contact list"
      width={1080}
      height={720}
    />
    <p>
      The preparation of the CV is a huge pain for new applicants. It requires a lot of effort and time and at the
      beginning of the path has little effect on the result. But the most part of the contact those years are
      fellow students with similar job requests. Thus, the copying CV of friends can help in compiling own.
    </p>

    <div style={`height: var(--space-section)`} />

    <Eyebrow as="h3">Contextual tips</Eyebrow>
    <p>Some applicants step into this experience for the first time. So there is a hypothesis that useful context tips can help:</p>
    <ul class="circle-list">
      <li>to choose the right vector at each stage of the funnel</li>
      <li>to help in advance to find the answer to the emerging issue</li>
      <li>to act more confidently in different situations.</li>
    </ul>
    <ContentMedia
      kind="video"
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-advice"
      alt="Contextual tips guiding the applicant through the funnel"
      width={1080}
      height={720}
    />
    <p>
      Fear of interviews causes anxiety and makes you doubt your own competence. It will be useful to read a
      couple of tips before going to an appointed interview.
    </p>
    <ContentMedia
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-advice-contact.png"
      alt="Interview tips shown before a scheduled appointment"
      width={2160}
      height={1440}
    />

    <div style={`height: var(--space-section)`} />

    <Eyebrow as="h3">Employer reviews</Eyebrow>
    <p>
      There is a huge process of finding potential employers. A significant part of this time is spent on the
      evaluation of a potential company. Feedback from job seekers about the employer can help at this stage to
      weed out unscrupulous companies.
    </p>
    <ContentMedia
      kind="video"
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-reviews"
      alt="Employer reviews shown to help evaluate potential employers"
      width={1080}
      height={720}
    />
    <p>
      Also, a large number of refusals affect the process of finding a potential job, because the subsequent
      depression reduces energy resources.
    </p>

    <div style={`height: var(--space-section)`} />

    <Eyebrow as="h3">Response timeout</Eyebrow>
    <p>Applicants can pre-tune to the appropriate expectations by being informed about the time of the decision duration of the employer.</p>
    <ContentMedia
      kind="video"
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-duration"
      alt="Expected response timeout shown to the applicant"
      width={1080}
      height={720}
    />

    <div style={`height: var(--space-section)`} />

    <Eyebrow as="h3">Personalization</Eyebrow>
    <p>Also, Avito can save previously entered requests and offer up-to-date suggestions in the root category to keep applicants in the context.</p>
    <ContentMedia
      kind="video"
      src="/casestudy/avito/avito-personalization"
      alt="Personalized suggestions based on previously entered requests"
      width={1080}
      height={720}
    />
  </ContentBlock>
</CaseStudyLayout>
